## Solution

**Setup and model.** Let the 8 Ciphers be $[8]=\{1,\dots,8\}$. Each of the $256=2^8$ servers corresponds to a unique subset $A(v)\subseteq[8]$ (the Ciphers it processes); the Hostile Ciphers of server $v$ are $[8]\setminus A(v)$. The drone includes each server independently with probability $1/2$ and then visits the included servers in a uniformly random order.

**Equivalent continuous model.** Assign to each server $u$ an independent priority $R_u\sim\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)$ and an independent inclusion bit $I_u\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(1/2)$. The drone visits exactly the servers with $I_u=1$, in increasing order of $R_u$. This is equivalent to the original "random subset + random order" process.

**Delay at a single server.** When the drone visits $v$ (so $I_v=1$), its library is $\bigcup_{u\text{ before }v}A(u)$, where "$u$ before $v$" means $I_u=1$ and $R_u<R_v$. The reboot delay at $v$ is
$$D(v)=\bigl|\{\,c\notin A(v):\exists\,u\text{ before }v\text{ with }c\in A(u)\,\}\bigr|.$$

By linearity of expectation,
$$\mathbb E[D(v)]=\Pr(v\in S)\sum_{c\notin A(v)}\Pr\bigl(c\text{ appears before }v\mid v\in S\bigr).$$

**Key probability.** Fix $v\in S$ and condition on $R_v=t$. For a Hostile cipher $c\notin A(v)$, the servers that process $c$ are exactly the $128=2^7$ subsets of $[8]$ containing $c$; none of them is $v$ (since $c\notin A(v)$). Each such server $u$ is before $v$ iff $I_u=1$ and $R_u<t$, which happens with probability $t/2$, independently across the $128$ servers. Hence
$$\Pr\bigl(c\text{ not before }v\mid v\in S,R_v=t\bigr)=(1-t/2)^{128}.$$
Integrating over $t$,
$$\Pr\bigl(c\text{ not before }v\mid v\in S\bigr)=\int_0^1(1-t/2)^{128}\,dt.$$
With $s=1-t/2$, $dt=-2\,ds$, the limits $t=0\to s=1$, $t=1\to s=1/2$:
$$\int_0^1(1-t/2)^{128}dt=2\int_{1/2}^{1}s^{128}ds=\frac{2}{129}\Bigl(1-2^{-129}\Bigr).$$
Therefore
$$\Pr\bigl(c\text{ appears before }v\mid v\in S\bigr)=1-\frac{2}{129}\bigl(1-2^{-129}\bigr).$$

**Summing over Hostile ciphers of $v$.** Since $\Pr(v\in S)=1/2$,
$$\mathbb E[D(v)]=\frac12\,(8-|A(v)|)\left[1-\frac{2}{129}\bigl(1-2^{-129}\bigr)\right].$$

**Summing over all servers.**
$$\sum_{v}\mathbb E[D(v)]=\frac12\left[1-\frac{2}{129}\bigl(1-2^{-129}\bigr)\right]\sum_{A\subseteq[8]}(8-|A|).$$
Using $\sum_{k=0}^{8}\binom{8}{k}(8-k)=8\cdot2^8-8\cdot2^7=2048-1024=1024$,
$$\mathbb E[\text{total delay}]=512\left[1-\frac{2}{129}\bigl(1-2^{-129}\bigr)\right].$$

**Simplification.**
$$=512\left[\frac{127}{129}+\frac{2^{-128}}{129}\right]=\frac{512\cdot127+2^{-119}}{129}=\frac{(2^{16}-2^9)\cdot2^{119}+1}{2^{119}\cdot129}=\frac{2^{135}-2^{128}+1}{2^{119}\cdot129}.$$

